01:00:30.192 --> 01:00:33.632
In fear of getting maybe, like, a little too technical on it, but it might be interesting

01:00:33.632 --> 01:00:39.992
to this audience, part of the way that we implement code mode is within a async context

01:00:39.992 --> 01:00:41.552
manager inside of Python.

01:00:41.552 --> 01:00:49.673
So that's, like, if you ever use, like, with, you know, the with context manager with some

01:00:49.673 --> 01:00:54.632
invocation of code as this other, you know, you get back this value variable that then

01:00:54.632 --> 01:00:57.113
you can call with inside that block.

01:00:57.113 --> 01:01:02.393
And what we actually do is that as the agents working, we don't actually perform any of

01:01:02.393 --> 01:01:05.312
those operations within the code mode block itself.

01:01:05.312 --> 01:01:09.692
They just are kind of, like, queued as a thing that the agent would like to do.

01:01:09.692 --> 01:01:15.132
And then when it exits code mode, we kind of see if we can reduce, like, simplify that

01:01:15.132 --> 01:01:18.013
invocation of code and replay it in such a way.

01:01:18.013 --> 01:01:20.972
Or we can do things like we can check the code that the agent's going to run prior to

01:01:20.972 --> 01:01:26.132
actually running it so that we can have high confidence that each transaction is, like,

01:01:26.132 --> 01:01:28.812
okay, prior to, like, actually playing it back in the UI.

01:01:28.812 --> 01:01:32.613
And so in terms of what Hadley was talking about, of giving this in context feedback,

01:01:32.613 --> 01:01:37.013
if the agent tries to do some sequence of API calls that were like, whoa, you shouldn't

01:01:37.013 --> 01:01:40.773
do that, we can actually just give it feedback that says you need to reverse or, like, change

01:01:40.773 --> 01:01:42.092
something about the API call.

01:01:42.092 --> 01:01:47.173
So we have this, like, little, like, level of indirection that allows us to inspect the

01:01:47.173 --> 01:01:51.333
thing that the agent's trying to do and, like, view it as a holistic chunk and then try to

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:54.852
give some sort of verifiable checks that tell the agent, like, oh, no, don't do that or

01:01:54.852 --> 01:01:56.572
do this.

